HISTORY closest to the bottom of the detector that is closest to the            HISTORY bottom of the slit (i.e. also closest to the bottom of the              HISTORY detector).  Moving up the detector, the FITS array is filled in         HISTORY with subsequent extraction apertures.  If no orders have been           HISTORY deselected in the extraction process, the contents of the ith           HISTORY aperture in order j can be found as follows:                            HISTORY lambda=array[*,0,{j-min(orders)}*naps + (i-1)],                         HISTORY flux=array[*,1,{j-min(orders)}*naps + (i-1)],                           HISTORY uncertainty=array[*,2,{j-min(orders)}*naps + (i-1)],                    HISTORY flag=array[*,3,{j-min(orders)}*naps + (i-1)].                           HISTORY                                                                         HISTORY The spectra in the file(s) spectra0007.fits, spectra0008.fits,          HISTORY spectra0009.fits, spectra0010.fits, spectra0011.fits,                   HISTORY spectra0012.fits were combined using a robust weighted mean             HISTORY with a sigma threshold of 8.  Aperture 1 modifications: The             HISTORY scale factors were determined using order 5 and are:                    HISTORY 0.9977550078139933, 1.0142536214329767, 1.0022551176289174,             HISTORY 0.9973074991374156, 1.007594197419939, 0.9953541374231977.              END                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             